{
  "requirement": "`habeas::validate_repository(root)` MUST return a report with the number of discovered requirements, the number of evidence files, and all validation errors for the supplied project. Ordinary invalid evidence MUST be reported in that report; an inaccessible project root MUST return an I/O error.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the requirement is met.**\n\n**Implementation (`src/evidence.rs`)**\n- `validate_repository(root)` (lines 119–122) is marked `{impl}`. It returns `io::Result<EvidenceReport>` by calling `inspect_repository(root)?.report`.\n- `EvidenceReport` (lines 16–23) is marked `{impl}`. It has `requirements`, `evidence_files` and `errors`.\n- The `examples` count is an extra field. It belongs to the shared `inspect_repository_with_progress` body, which is also marked `{impl}` for `requirements.examples.evidence`. I do not treat it as unspecified behaviour.\n- `inspect_repository` and `inspect_repository_with_progress` (lines 159–301) are marked `{impl}`. They fill the report:\n  - `requirements` counts only declarations of kind `Requirement`.\n  - `evidence_files` is the number of JSON files discovered under `evidence/`.\n  - `errors` collects everything: workspace configuration, book source, definition, evidence file, orphan, missing-evidence, reference and Rust-coverage problems.\n- Ordinary invalid evidence is pushed into `errors`, not returned as an `Err`. This covers invalid JSON, orphans, a false determination and changed text.\n- The only `?` that can produce an `Err` in the top-level flow is `fs::canonicalize(root)?`, at the start of `inspect_repository_with_progress`. It fails for an inaccessible project root, which gives the required I/O error. The other failures are turned into report errors.\n- The public API is re-exported in `src/lib.rs` (`pub use evidence::{EvidenceReport, validate_repository}`). `validate()` consumes the report's counts and errors.\n\n**Tests**\n- `inaccessible_project_root_is_an_io_error_not_a_report` (`tests/evidence_boundaries.rs`) checks that a missing root returns `Err` with `ErrorKind::NotFound`. It also checks that broken evidence in an accessible root appears in `report.errors`, so the failure boundary is covered both ways.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` checks that many different kinds of invalid evidence are all collected into one report.\n- `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` checks `report.requirements == 1` and `report.evidence_files == 1` with no errors.\n- `inspection_progress_preserves_validation_and_finishes_each_phase` compares the report counts and errors between `inspect_repository` and the progress variant, in both a valid and an invalid repository.\n- `tests/commands.rs::fixme_fixture` checks a clean report for a fixture containing FIXME determinations.\n- `discovered_external_cargo_outputs_validate_freshness_and_obey_disallow` checks that stale and disallowed inputs appear as report errors.\n\n**Gaps:** none found. Implementation markers are complete, and the tests cover the counts, error aggregation, and the I/O error boundary.",
